  "notes": [
    "Exercises the ten public desktop-socket notification v2 methods and seven CLI entry points against one deterministic workspace/surface fixture.",
    "Each id-targeted case clears and reseeds the notification store before resolving the generated notification UUID from notification.list, avoiding assumptions about UUIDs or retained ordering.",
    "The lane covers payloads, defaults, selector validation, caller preference and fallback routing, targeted delivery identity, not-found behavior, read/dismiss/clear mutations, target navigation, CLI help and output, state probes, and lifecycle events.",
    "notification.reconcile is intentionally excluded because canonical exposes it through the authenticated mobile-host RPC rather than the desktop control socket.",
    "Pointer-scoped equivalences cover only the isolated capture working directory and the pre-existing selected bootstrap surface, whose canonical UUID maps to the stable Windows legacy id surface-1; all notification behavior and remaining fields stay strict."
  ],
